+## Configured training environment
+
+The original machine used the yao-rl Conda environment at /home/autel/miniforge3/envs/yao-rl with Python 3.11, PyTorch 2.7.0+cu126, mjlab 1.2.0, mujoco-warp 3.8.1, and warp-lang 1.12.0. The project was installed in editable mode and the observation manager matched the bundled patch.
+
+Run the following in the project directory when opening a new terminal:
+
+```bash
+cd /home/autel/AMP_mjlab_wmac
+source scripts/activate_env.sh
+python scripts/list_envs.py --keyword AMP
+python scripts/train.py Unitree-G1-AMP-Flat --env.scene.num-envs 4096
+```
+
+The activation script selects the existing environment, sets MUJOCO_GL=egl, and prepends the repository to PYTHONPATH so the local AMP fork of rsl_rl is imported. The existing rsl-rl-lib==5.0.1 distribution satisfies mjlab; no second editable installation of rsl_rl is needed on that machine.
+
+On other machines use AMP_CONDA_ENV to select an environment and AMP_CONDA_ROOT to select a Conda installation. With no root specified, the script checks the active Conda, then the usual locations under the home directory.
+
+Short training check (exits when complete):
+
+```bash
+python scripts/train.py Unitree-G1-AMP-Flat \
+  --env.scene.num-envs 16 --agent.max-iterations 2 \
+  --agent.num-steps-per-env 8 --agent.algorithm.num-learning-epochs 1 \
+  --agent.run-name env_smoke
+```
+
+TensorBoard is the default logger and requires no Weights & Biases login. View the training curves with:
+
+```bash
+tensorboard --logdir logs/rsl_rl/g1_amp_locomotion --port 6006
+```
